docs-check	Boundary-unit naming ratchet	2026-09-22T14:16:04.5584706Z hdl/ieee1722/aaf/KL_chan_map_capture.sv:KL_chan_map_capture: lb_flush_i — documented in samples, not named for it: bind wipe / stream-table eviction pulse per RX stream: empties the stream's pair queues, un-primes them and zeroes its holds, so no stale samples replay on a rebind. Defaulted off: an integration without a bind plane keeps the free-running behaviour.
docs-check	Boundary-unit naming ratchet	2026-09-22T14:16:04.5588142Z hdl/ieee1722/aaf/KL_chan_map_render.sv:KL_chan_map_render: map_flat_o — documented in bytes, not named for it: --- whole-map export (combinational; entry p = [p*8 +: 8]) ------------ The AEM GET_AUDIO_MAP answer walks a PAGE of entries in one query window, and the single readback port above is owned by the CSR CHMAP_SNAP path; the map is N_PHYS_P bytes of flops, so exporting it whole is wires, not logic, and keeps the two readers independent - which is exactly what lets a testbench compare them against each other.
